# crypto-llm-alpaca

Paper-only crypto trading research system using Alpaca, structured LLM features, SQLite audit trails, and rule-based execution.

The LLM is a feature extractor, not the trader. The decision engine combines validated LLM sentiment with technical features and risk gates. V1 defaults to offline-safe mock LLM behavior and refuses Alpaca paper actions unless paper credentials are present.

## Quick start

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python -m pytest

cp .env.example .env       # then fill in keys (see Environment below)
crypto-llm doctor          # preflight: env, keys, DB, config
crypto-llm init-db
crypto-llm backfill --demo                   # or: --days 365 --timeframe 1Hour for real bars
crypto-llm ingest-news
crypto-llm extract-signals
crypto-llm build-features
crypto-llm backtest --strategy adaptive-breakout --persist
crypto-llm dashboard       # multipage Streamlit UI
```

## Environment

`.env` is auto-loaded from the repo root at every CLI invocation. Process env wins on conflict.

```
APCA_API_KEY_ID=
APCA_API_SECRET_KEY=
APCA_API_BASE_URL=https://paper-api.alpaca.markets
HUGGINGFACE_API_TOKEN=
HF_MODEL=meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct
OPENAI_API_KEY=
```

No live trading endpoint or live order mode is implemented in v1. The broker class refuses any base URL without `paper-api`.

## CLI commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `init-db` | Create / migrate the SQLite schema. |
| `doctor [--json]` | Preflight checks: `.env`, Alpaca keys + reachability, HF token + preflight call, config loadable, DB schema, bar count. Exit 1 if any FAIL. |
| `ingest-news` | Fetch RSS feeds from `data.rss_feeds`, dedupe, store in `news_items`. |
| `extract-signals [--limit N]` | Run the configured LLM provider over unscored news, write `llm_signals`. |
| `backfill [--demo] [--days N] [--start ISO] [--end ISO] [--timeframe TF]` | Fetch Alpaca crypto bars (or generate demo bars) into `bars`. |
| `build-features` | Compute per-bar `strategy_features` for every symbol. |
| `rank-setups [--limit N]` | Rank current setups by signal strength. |
| `quality-growth-candidates [--limit N] [--signal-limit N] [--narrative-news-limit N] [--explain]` | Rank profiled smaller projects by project quality, DefiLlama TVL/fee data when enabled, narrative rotation from attributed news, 4H/daily/weekly trend alignment, latest momentum/volume, and stored sentiment vectors. `--explain` prints a readable thesis/checklist report. |
| `paper-candidates [--limit N]` | List symbols whose latest features pass the entry gate. |
| `backtest --strategy {demo,breakout-volume,adaptive-breakout,quality-growth} [--equity F] [--demo] [--all-bars] [--summary] [--persist]` | Run a backtest; `--all-bars` uses the full stored history, `--summary` keeps stdout compact, and `--persist` writes `backtest_runs/trades/equity_curve`. |
| `sweep [--equity F] [--top N] [--demo]` | Focused parameter sweep over `adaptive-breakout`; persists every run. |
| `paper-once [--symbol S] [--equity F] [--submit] [--demo-only]` | Build one paper decision; `--submit` calls the Alpaca paper API. |
| `paper-loop --iterations N [...same as paper-once]` | Run `paper-once` logic N times in one session. |
| `report` | Print row counts for every table. |
| `dashboard` | Launch the multipage Streamlit UI (see below). |

`--config PATH` is a global flag accepted by every subcommand and defaults to `config/default.yaml`.

## Dashboard (multipage UI)

```powershell
crypto-llm dashboard
```

Pages:

- **Home** — DB row counts, env-var presence, last 5 backtest runs.
- **Strategy Lab** — sortable backtest-run table, candle chart with buy/sell markers, trades, open positions, equity curve. Forms at the top trigger a new backtest or focused sweep via subprocess; results auto-refresh on success.
- **Parameters** — live YAML editor for every config section. **Save & reload** writes `config/ui_overrides.yaml` and every other UI page picks it up automatically. The default file is never modified. **Discard overrides** removes the file.
- **News & Signals** — latest news + signals tables; buttons trigger `ingest-news` and `extract-signals`.
- **Doctor** — runs `crypto-llm doctor --json` and renders a pass/warn/fail list.

The UI is a thin client over the CLI: every action shells out to `python -m crypto_llm_alpaca.cli ...`, so the CLI remains the source of truth.

## LLM providers

Default `llm.provider` is `mock` (deterministic, offline). Switch in `config/default.yaml` (or via the Parameters page):

```yaml
llm:
  provider: "huggingface"   # or "openai" or "mock"
  model: "meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct"
```

Both real providers read their key from env (`HUGGINGFACE_API_TOKEN`/`HF_TOKEN`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`). `crypto-llm doctor` will preflight HF when configured.

## Strategy lab

Three research paths:

- `breakout-volume` — breakout + volume / range confirmation.
- `adaptive-breakout` — volatility-aware momentum. ATR stops + trailing, signal-strength ranking, `top_n_per_bar` cap, risk-sized entries. The focused sweep tests breakout lookback, relative volume, ATR stop/trail multiples, and top-N selection.
- `quality-growth` — smaller-project research strategy. Requires an editable project profile (`quality`, `growth`, `backer`, `liquidity`, and `risk` scores), then demands momentum, relative volume, volume acceleration, and positive higher-timeframe trend before entry. `config/quality_growth.yaml` keeps hourly bars for execution/risk, derives 4H/daily/weekly confirmation from those bars, evaluates new entries on 4-hour decision intervals, enriches current candidates with cache-first DefiLlama TVL/fee data and narrative rotation from stored news, and uses wider ATR exits plus 1x/2x/5x partial-profit targets for longer holds.

```powershell
crypto-llm --config config/quality_growth.yaml backfill --days 730 --timeframe 1Hour
crypto-llm --config config/quality_growth.yaml ingest-news
crypto-llm --config config/quality_growth.yaml extract-signals --limit 40
crypto-llm --config config/quality_growth.yaml quality-growth-candidates
crypto-llm --config config/quality_growth.yaml quality-growth-candidates --explain
crypto-llm --config config/quality_growth.yaml backtest --strategy quality-growth --all-bars --summary --persist
```

## Risk defaults

- Crypto, hourly cadence.
- Max total open notional exposure: 30% of equity.
- Target concurrent positions: 3-5.
- Initial stop loss: 1%.
- Take-profit ladder: 25% at +10%, 25% at +20%, 50% at +50%.
- After TP1 fills, remaining stop moves to breakeven.
- New entries stop after 5% paper-equity drawdown in 24h.

## Data → decision flow

1. `ingest-news` pulls RSS, dedupes by hash.
2. `extract-signals` turns news into structured `llm_signals` rows (sentiment, confidence, horizon, event_type, rationale). Curated article symbols and the configured universe stay authoritative so BTC/ETH cannot leak into smaller-project signals unless they are actually article symbols.
3. `backfill` stores Alpaca crypto bars.
4. `build-features` (or per-bar in backtest) computes breakout, relative volume, range expansion, momentum, HTF trend, 4H/daily/weekly trend alignment, ATR / ATR regime, expected move, signal strength.
5. `quality-growth-candidates` optionally enriches the latest ranking with DefiLlama free API data (`/protocols`, `/summary/fees/{protocol}`) cached under `data/cache`, plus narrative labels/momentum from stored news.
6. `backtest --persist` writes runs/trades/equity curves to SQLite.
7. `paper-once` builds one decision per symbol; `--submit` is the only path that calls the Alpaca paper API.

## Autopilot

`crypto-llm autopilot` is the morning entry point. It:

1. Pulls account equity + open positions from Alpaca paper.
2. Builds a decision per symbol in the universe (signals + technical features + risk gate).
3. Persists every decision to the `decisions` table (audit trail).
4. Submits **bracket orders** (entry + TP + SL) for the top-N accepted decisions, capped by `--max-trades` and `--max-positions`. Falls back to split orders if Alpaca crypto rejects bracket.
5. Writes `outputs/YYYY-MM-DD.md` summarizing decisions + fills + errors and upserts a `daily_reports` row.

```powershell
# First week — dry run, no orders submitted
crypto-llm autopilot --dry-run --max-trades 3

# Live (Alpaca paper)
crypto-llm autopilot --max-trades 3 --max-positions 5
```

Flags: `--dry-run`, `--max-trades N` (default 3), `--max-positions N` (default 5), `--symbols A,B,C` (override), `--equity F` (override), `--demo-only`.

### Schedule daily 9 AM (Windows Task Scheduler)

```powershell
# From repo root
schtasks /create /xml scripts\CryptoLLMAutopilot.xml /tn CryptoLLMAutopilot

# Verify
schtasks /query /tn CryptoLLMAutopilot

# Manual fire (test the wiring)
schtasks /run /tn CryptoLLMAutopilot
type outputs\logs\autopilot-*.log
```

The XML points at `scripts\autopilot_morning.cmd` which auto-uses `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` if present, else system `python`. Logs land in `outputs\logs\autopilot-YYYYMMDD.log`. Markdown reports land in `outputs\YYYY-MM-DD.md`.

When claude.ai routines are back up:
```
/schedule create --cron "0 9 * * *" --command "crypto-llm autopilot --max-trades 3"
```

### Backtest the autopilot logic over historical bars

`crypto-llm autopilot-backtest` replays the morning-decision loop on stored bars. Default mode = technical + risk gate only (no LLM signals — RSS history is shallow). Optional `--synthetic-signals` samples sentiment from a normal distribution for stress testing.

```powershell
# 1. Backfill 1-3 years of bars (one-time, ~5-15 min over Alpaca)
crypto-llm backfill --days 1095 --timeframe 1Hour

# 2. Run the backtest (no LLM signals = path A, what we trust)
crypto-llm autopilot-backtest --start 2023-01-01 --persist

# 3. Optional: synthetic signal stress test (path B, sanity check only)
crypto-llm autopilot-backtest --start 2023-01-01 --synthetic-signals --persist

# 4. Review in Strategy Lab UI
crypto-llm dashboard   # filter by strategy = "autopilot"
```

Flags: `--start ISO`, `--end ISO`, `--equity F`, `--max-trades N`, `--max-positions N`, `--take-profit F`, `--stop-loss F`, `--synthetic-signals`, `--seed N`, `--persist`.

What gets simulated per morning:
1. Score every symbol with `compute_features` + (optional) synthetic signal.
2. Apply risk gate.
3. Top-N accepted by score, capped by `max_trades_per_day` and `max_positions`.
4. Bracket fill simulation: enter at next bar's open; walk forward; SL touch wins ties (conservative); TP touch closes win; otherwise stays open until end of data.

Honest limitation: real LLM-signal replay needs historical news (CryptoPanic API, archive). Without it, the backtest tests the strategy + bracket logic, not the news-driven sentiment edge. Real edge measurement = let the live bot run for 6+ months and replay against the accumulated `news_items` + `llm_signals` tables.

### UI for autopilot

- **Daily Reports** page — list of runs, view markdown for any date, trigger an ad-hoc run.
- **Live Positions** page — live Alpaca positions + open orders + bracket children.
- **Decisions Audit** page — date picker, every decision (accepted + rejected) with score/conf/reason; CSV download.

## Optional TradingView workflow

A premium TradingView Desktop account can be used as a human-in-the-loop analysis surface to compare signals and iterate Pine strategies. It is intentionally not part of the v1 execution path; Alpaca paper remains the only order rail.
